.TH DIFFVIM 1 "2026-08-18" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim \- animate a code diff in vim as if a human were typing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-multi
.RI <old1:new1>
.RI <old2:new2>
\&...

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-replay
.RI <file>
.RB [ \-\-from
.IR REV ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR REV ]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-git-rev
.IR REV..REV
.RI <file>
[<file> ...]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-diff
.IR FILE
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]

.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-version
.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim
opens the old version of a file in vim and animates the transformation into
the new version character by character. The cursor glides between change
locations with smooth ease-in-out acceleration, and only the actually-changed
characters are deleted and re-typed \(em surrounding text is never touched.

After the animation completes (or the user stops it), the buffer is a normal
vim buffer and can be edited, saved, or quit normally. By default the buffer
is marked as not modified so
.B :q
quits cleanly; use
.B --keep-dirty
to leave the buffer modified (then
.B :q!
is required).

Three implementations are available:
.TP
.B diffvim
Bash launcher + embedded Vimscript engine. Uses vim's native
.BR timer_start ()
for async animation. No external dependencies beyond vim 8+. Best for
everyday use.
.TP
.B diffvim-tmux
Bash orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Bash sends Ex commands to vim via
.BR tmux\ send-keys .
Requires bash 4+, tmux 3+, vim 8+, diff, sed, awk.
.TP
.B diffvim.pl
Perl orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Same architecture as diffvim-tmux
but with pluggable diff parser modules. Requires Perl 5.10+, tmux 3+, vim 8+.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Core Options

.TP
.BR \-\-speed\  N
Speed multiplier.
.B 0.5
= half speed,
.B 2
= double speed,
.B 5
= 5x speed.
All timing delays are divided by this value.
Also settable via
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
environment variable.

.TP
.BI \-\-output\  FILE
After the animation completes, write the buffer to
.I FILE
and quit vim. Also works with
.B q
(quit) \(em the buffer is written before stopping.

.TP
.BR \-\-scroll\  zz | zt | zb | none
Scroll the cursor to the specified position during animation:
.RS
.TP 4
.B zz
Center cursor on screen
.TP 4
.B zt
Cursor at top of screen
.TP 4
.B zb
Cursor at bottom of screen
.TP 4
.B none
Don't force scroll (default)
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-multi
Treat arguments as
.I old:new
pairs for multi-file animation. After finishing one file, the animation
transitions to the next.

.TP
.BI \-\-context\  N
Fold unchanged regions longer than 2*N lines, keeping N lines of context
around each hunk. Default: 0 (no folding).

.TP
.B Compute tool selection
The C++ compute tool
.I compute/bin/diffvim-compute-cpp
is the default and is searched for in
.IR compute/bin/ ,
.IR /usr/local/bin/ ,
and
.IR ~/.local/bin/ .
If found, diffvim pre-computes the diff before launching vim (10-100x
faster than the in-vim patience diff for large files). If not found, diffvim
falls back to the embedded vimscript patience diff
.RI ( s:LineDiff / s:CharDiff )
with a warning on stderr. (The
.B --tool
flag that used to select between C/C++/Rust/Go compute tools has been
removed.)

.TP
.B \-\-precomputed FILE
Use a pre-computed diff from FILE (typically produced by
.BR diffvim-compute-cpp (1)).
Bypasses the in-vim patience diff entirely.

.SS Unified Options

These are the recommended option selectors. Each replaces multiple
individual flags from earlier versions.

.TP
.BR \-\-delete-pacing\  char | rapid-eol | rapid-identical | accel | word | instant
Unified deletion strategy (default:
.BR word ).
.IP \(bu 3
.B char
\(em one char at a time
.IP \(bu 3
.B rapid-eol
\(em rapid shot at end of line
.IP \(bu 3
.B rapid-identical
\(em accelerate identical char runs
.IP \(bu 3
.B accel
\(em accelerate through long runs
.IP \(bu 3
.B word
\(em word-by-word with acceleration (default; char→word→rapid progression)
.IP \(bu 3
.B instant
\(em all strategies enabled (fastest)

.TP
.BR \-\-delete-speed\  slow | normal | fast | instant
Deletion speed multiplier (default:
.BR normal ).
.B fast
halves all delete delays;
.B instant
sets them to 1ms.

.TP
.BI \-\-delete-threshold \ N
Minimum chars to trigger rapid/word modes (default: 3).

.TP
.BR \-\-insert-pacing\  char | word | accel
Unified insertion strategy (default:
.BR char ).
.IP \(bu 3
.B char
\(em one char at a time
.IP \(bu 3
.B word
\(em batch short words (<=8 chars) instantly
.IP \(bu 3
.B accel
\(em accelerate char-by-char inserts

.TP
.BR \-\-insert-speed\  slow | normal | fast
Insertion speed multiplier (default:
.BR normal ).
.B fast
halves TYPE_DELAY_MS and WORD_PAUSE_MS.

.TP
.BR \-\-pacing\  uniform | adaptive | gaussian | review
Unified timing mode (default:
.BR uniform ).
.IP \(bu 3
.B uniform
\(em fixed delays, no jitter
.IP \(bu 3
.B adaptive
\(em slow down in complex regions
.IP \(bu 3
.B gaussian
\(em add human-like timing jitter
.IP \(bu 3
.B review
\(em pause every 5 lines in large hunks

.TP
.BR \-\-highlight\  none | inline | word | hunk
Unified highlight mode (default:
.BR none ).
.IP \(bu 3
.B none
\(em no highlighting
.IP \(bu 3
.B inline
\(em paint freshly typed/deleted chars
.IP \(bu 3
.B word
\(em highlight the word at cursor before change
.IP \(bu 3
.B hunk
\(em highlight the entire hunk

.SS Diff Options

.TP
.BR \-\-parser\  perl
(diffvim.pl only) Diff parser to use. Only
.B perl
is supported (pure-Perl Patience algorithm, no external dependencies).
The flag is accepted for backwards compatibility but has no effect
since the diff2html parser was removed.

.TP
.B \-\-word-diff
Use word-level diff instead of char-level. Groups changes by word
(non-space sequences), producing more natural typing patterns.

.TP
.B \-\-algorithm
Deprecated. Patience diff is now the only algorithm. The flag is accepted
for backward compatibility but has no effect.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-hunk-chars\  N
If a hunk has more than N changed characters, skip the char-by-char
animation and apply the entire hunk instantly.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-line-len\  N
Warn if any line exceeds N characters (char-level diff may be slow).
Default: 10000.

.SS Git Options

.TP
.B \-\-replay
Animate git history for the given file(s). For each commit in the range,
extracts the old version and animates the transformation to the next commit.

.TP
.BI \-\-from\  REV
Git revision to start replay from. Default:
.BR HEAD~5 .

.TP
.BI \-\-to\  REV
Git revision to end replay at. Default:
.BR HEAD .

.TP
.BI \-\-git-rev\  REV..REV
Animate a git commit range using
.I REV..REV
syntax. Shorthand for
.B \-\-replay \-\-from REV1 \-\-to REV2.

.TP
.B \-\-git-blame
Show git blame information for each changed line.

.SH CONTROLS
During animation, the following keys are active in vim normal mode:

.SS Basic Controls
.TP
.B <Space>
Pause / resume the animation. In
.B \-\-step-mode ,
advances one char op instead.
.TP
.B n
Skip current hunk: apply all remaining character operations instantly,
then pause for review. Press
.B n
again to advance to the next hunk. This is the "review mode" \(em apply
one hunk at a time, pausing between each.
.TP
.B b
Back to previous hunk: revert the buffer to the state before the
current hunk started and replay it from the beginning.
.TP
.B q
Stop the animation. By default the buffer is then marked as not modified
so
.B :q
quits cleanly. Use
.B \-\-keep-dirty
to require
.B :q!
instead.

.SS Speed Controls
.TP
.B +
Speed up: multiply the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B \-
Slow down: divide the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B =
Reset speed to 1.0x.

.SS Multi-File Navigation
.TP
.B ]
Next file (in multi-file mode). Applies all remaining hunks instantly
and loads the next file pair.
.TP
.B [
Previous file (in multi-file mode). Loads the previous file pair.

.SS Granular Navigation
.TP
.B B
(Shift-B) Go back one char op.
.TP
.B N
(Shift-N) Skip to next file (multi-file mode).
.TP
.B Ctrl-B
Go back to the beginning.
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
Skip to the end.

.SS Undo/Redo
.TP
.B u
Undo last hunk (revert to previous snapshot).
.TP
.B Ctrl-r
Redo hunk.

.SS Display
.TP
.B ?
Toggle full-screen help overlay.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fold on/off (with
.BR \-\-context ).

.SS Progress
A progress message is shown in the vim status line:
.RS
.PP
.nf
diffvim: hunk 3/7 (42%) | speed 2.3x | PAUSED
.fi
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
All options can be set via
.B DIFFVIM_<OPTION_NAME>
environment variables. Command-line options override environment
variables, which override built-in defaults.

.SS Core Timing
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TICK_MS
Animation frame interval in milliseconds (default: 16, ~60fps).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TYPE_DELAY_MS
Delay between typed characters in milliseconds (default: 50).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_DELAY_MS
Delay between deleted characters in milliseconds (default: 40).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MIN_MS
Minimum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 250).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MAX_MS
Maximum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 1600).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MS_PER_UNIT
Milliseconds per unit of glide distance (default: 6). Lines are weighted
80x more than columns.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HUNK_PAUSE_MS
Pause between hunks in milliseconds (default: 250).

.SS Unified Selectors
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_PACING
Deletion strategy (default: word).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_SPEED
Deletion speed (default: normal).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_THRESHOLD
Min chars to trigger rapid/word modes (default: 3).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_INSERT_PACING
Insertion strategy (default: char).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_INSERT_SPEED
Insertion speed (default: normal).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_PACING
Timing mode (default: uniform).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT
Highlight mode (default: none).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_COLOR
Highlight group (default: DiffChange).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_DURATION_MS
Highlight duration in ms (default: 1000).

.SS Other
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
Speed multiplier (default: 1.0). Same as
.BR \-\-speed .
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MAX_LINE_LEN
Warn threshold for long lines (default: 10000).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_KEEP_DIRTY
Set to
.B 1
to leave the buffer modified after animation.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_PRESET
Default preset to apply (same as
.BR \-\-preset ).

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic Usage
.PP
.nf
diffvim old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Speed Control
.PP
.nf
# Half speed for a presentation
diffvim \-\-speed 0.5 old.py new.py

# 3x speed for quick review
diffvim \-\-speed 3 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Output
.PP
.nf
# Write result to file and quit
diffvim \-\-output result.py old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Display Options
.PP
.nf
# Center cursor, highlight hunks, fold unchanged regions
diffvim \-\-scroll zz \-\-highlight hunk \-\-context 0 old.py new.py

# High-contrast theme
diffvim \-\-theme high-contrast old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Diff Algorithms
.PP
.nf
# Use patience diff for more human-readable hunks
diffvim \-\-algorithm patience old.py new.py

# Word-level diff
diffvim \-\-word-diff old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Unified Options
.PP
.nf
# Deletion strategy: word-by-word with acceleration
diffvim \-\-delete-pacing word old.py new.py

# Fast deletion for large refactors
diffvim \-\-delete-pacing instant \-\-delete-speed fast old.py new.py

# Insertion strategy: batch short words
diffvim \-\-insert-pacing word old.py new.py

# Timing: human-like jitter
diffvim \-\-pacing gaussian old.py new.py

# Timing: pause every 5 lines for review
diffvim \-\-pacing review old.py new.py

# Highlight freshly typed/deleted chars
diffvim \-\-highlight inline old.py new.py

# Highlight the entire hunk before animating
diffvim \-\-highlight hunk old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Buffer State After Animation
.PP
.nf
# Default: ':q' quits cleanly (buffer marked not modified)
diffvim old.py new.py

# Keep buffer modified; ':q!' required to quit
diffvim \-\-keep-dirty old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Multi-file Animation
.PP
.nf
diffvim \-\-multi old1.py:new1.py old2.py:new2.py
.fi

.SS Git Integration
.PP
.nf
# Replay last 5 commits of a file
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py

# Specific commit range
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py \-\-from v1.0 \-\-to HEAD

# Using \-\-git-rev syntax
diffvim \-\-git-rev HEAD~3..HEAD src/main.py

# Show git blame during animation
diffvim \-\-git-blame old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Unified Diff Input
.PP
.nf
# Animate from a patch file
diffvim \-\-diff my.patch

# From stdin
git diff | diffvim \-\-diff \-
.fi

.SS Debugging
.PP
.nf
# Dry run (print ops without launching vim)
diffvim \-\-dry-run old.py new.py

# Verbose logging
diffvim \-\-debug old.py new.py
cat /tmp/diffvim-debug.log

# Compare parsers
diffvim \-\-parser-compare old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Vim Plugin
.PP
.nf
# Inside an existing vim session:
:Diffvim old.py new.py
:Diffvim old.py new.py tabnew
.fi

